    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with **Kyle Tucker** serving as our clear focal point. Boasting a 66.85 efficiency score, **Kyle Tucker** sits comfortably in our \"Strong\" tier against Landen Roupp. While Roupp isn't a pushover, the matchup allows **Kyle Tucker** to capitalize on a favorable SP_xERA of 4.07. Supporting him is **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (59.35), who benefits from a high-upside combination of a wind-aided park factor (+5%) and a significant dynamic platoon advantage (+14%) against Corbin Burnes. Despite the difficulty of facing an ace like Burnes, **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** remains a must-start given his current form and the premium we place on his speed-centric profile in our 5x5 build.\n\nThe final roster spot in the OF saw a tight contest, with **Andy Pages** (58.80) narrowly edging out our remaining bench options. While **Andy Pages** faces the moderate challenge of an elite defensive catcher behind the plate, his projected cleanup role and the matchup against Roupp provided the necessary floor to suppress the variance of our marginal bench assets. We are closely monitoring the status of **Drake Baldwin**, **Sam Antonacci**, **Heliot Ramos**, **Dominic Smith**, and **Miguel Vargas**; as \"Lineup Pending\" designations, these scores are heavily sensitive to final manager card submissions. **Sam Antonacci** is of particular interest; despite a negative platoon adjustment (-9%), his elite xwOBA of 0.403 suggests he is primed to outperform his base projection if he secures that leadoff spot.\n\nRisks remain on the periphery, particularly with the bottom of our order. **Nasim Nunez** (45.88), **Brady House** (47.59), and **Dominic Smith** (41.51) are all flirting with the sub-40 \"Below Floor\" threshold, largely due to the stiff competition from Burnes and Ben Brown. We are managing these game caps carefully; should any of these players be dropped down the order in final lineups, we will not hesitate to pull them to preserve our season-long limits. Elsewhere, we remain in a holding pattern with **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** and **Gunnar Henderson**, both of whom are unavailable today, while **Luis Robert Jr.** remains sidelined on the IL, leaving us to navigate a high-stakes day without our core power anchors.",
